      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"future-proofing\" angle, but they're pretty savvy. If I just say \"you're doing great, but you should spend more money to stay that way,\" they're gonna call BS and tell us we're just upselling.\n\nCan we be a bit more specific? Is there any way to point to certain \"potential\" vulnerabilities or specific types of advanced attacks that their current setup wouldn't catch, even if the audit didn't actually find any active issues? I need something more concrete to show them they're actually at risk.",
